sa. He often sought to forge alliances to protect Tripoli from external threats. He also engaged in diplomatic negotiations with Muslim rulers attempting to secure favorable treaties and trade agreements. His diplomatic efforts were often complex and involved navigating the competing interests of various powers. He skillfully used diplomacy to maintain a balance of power in the region.\n\nRaymond III's reign ended tragically in 1131. He was assassinated by his own nephew a rival claimant to the throne. His death plunged the Tripoli County into a period of instability and conflict. Despite the challenges he faced Raymond III left a lasting legacy as a strong and effective ruler who played a significant role in the history of the Crusades. His reign is remembered for its military successes its territorial expansion and its contributions to the economic and cultural development of the Tripoli County. He is considered one of the most important rulers of the Tripoli County's history.\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Raymond", "logprob": -0.14342188835144043}, {"token": "▁III", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Count", "logprob": -4.5060096454108134e-05}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -2.50339189733495e-06}, {"token": "▁Tripoli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁was", "logprob": -0.0798519179224968}, {"token": "▁a", "logprob": -0.04111293703317642}, {"token": "▁powerful", "logprob": -0.5501455068588257}, {"token": "▁ruler", "logprob": -0.6038829684257507}, {"token": "▁who", "logprob": -0.6161623597145081}, {"token": "▁reigned", "logprob": -0.5910662412643433}, {"token": "▁from", "logprob": -1.2193617820739746}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": -0.0020070187747478485}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -9.786603914108127e-05}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.0011750705307349563}, {"token": "0", "logprob": -1.862494707107544}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.01235545426607132}, {"token": "▁to", "logprob": -0.011992614716291428}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": -0.00039843725971877575}, {"token": 